{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ככל אשר שאלת", :translit "k'khol asher sha'alta", :gloss "according to all that you asked"} {:he "ככל עולה ע'", :translit "k'khol olah 'ayin", :gloss "according to all that rises [equals] seventy"} {:he "ע' זקנים", :translit "'ayin z'kenim", :gloss "seventy elders"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ככל עולה", :b "ע'"}], :frame {:text "At the Sinaitic revelation the people requested that Moses serve as intermediary rather than hearing directly from God, as stated at Deuteronomy 5:20–24. In response, God established a framework of leadership. Numbers 11:16 records God's instruction to gather seventy elders of Israel. The midrashic tradition in Tanchuma connects Israel's request at Sinai to the appointment of these elders, reading Deuteronomy 18:16 as a direct consequence. Ba'al HaTurim extends this pattern: the gematria equating 'ככל עולה' with seventy demonstrates that just as God granted the seventy elders in response to Israel's request at Sinai, so too when Israel request prophets in the future, their request is granted.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 5:20–24" "Numbers 11:16" "Tanchuma Shoftim"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ככל עולה", :a-value 181, :b "ע'", :b-value 70, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:37:24.138660862Z", :model "glm-5.2"}